# Arch/Manjaro repo packages — the pacman half of homebrew/Brewfile.
#
# One name per line; # starts a comment. Read by install-linux.sh, which feeds
# the whole list to `pacman -S --needed` in one transaction.
#
# NOT VERIFIED AGAINST A LIVE MIRROR. This list was transcribed from the
# Brewfile on a Mac, so the names are Arch's as best known rather than as
# confirmed by `pacman -Si`. install-linux.sh checks every name before it
# installs anything and prints the ones pacman does not recognise instead of
# failing the run, so the first execution on a real machine is what turns this
# comment into a settled list. Move anything it rejects to arch/aurlist or fix
# the spelling here.
#
# Deliberately NOT a translation of the cask list. Those are 90 macOS apps;
# picking Linux desktop equivalents is a per-app decision, not a mapping, and
# guessing at it here would install a lot of software nobody asked for.

